#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362389 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2bfe9eb7-0858-52db-9dfb-831c6cfdd93e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361032} {:answer/id #uuid "92da08bc-b94a-5969-b999-e830f9be45bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361489} {:answer/id #uuid "d820da19-1020-5cd4-ad52-3b72b70b868e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361798} {:answer/id #uuid "dda5046b-7496-5105-85c6-0e609a2a6b0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361825} {:answer/id #uuid "e3499b31-131f-5fed-9b53-def82bb10a5d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361854}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186361854} :answer-field/id #uuid "7631dea4-74c6-5439-9236-5c814d4472e7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362080}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "3e095599-c87c-5424-992d-faffcd2cd697" :question/math-academy-id "q-9980" :question/problem "The entry ${a}_{21}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & k & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nequals $\\frac{2}{5}.$ Find the value of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & k & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & =2\\begin{vmatrix}k & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix}-3\\begin{vmatrix}4 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{vmatrix}+1\\begin{vmatrix}4 & k \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2(k-2)-3(4-6)+1(4-3k) \\\\  & =2k-4+6+4-3k \\\\  & =6-k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{21}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{12}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{12} & =(-1)^{1+2}\\begin{vmatrix}4 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-\\begin{vmatrix}4 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-(4-6) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{21}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6-k}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{6-k}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{21}^{′}=\\frac{2}{5}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{6-k} & =\\frac{2}{5} \\\\ 2\\cdot 5 & =2(6-k) \\\\ 10 & =12-2k \\\\ 2k & =2 \\\\ k & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362402 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "360fced2-8218-5819-b49f-a6bdb1fc1bee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361080} {:answer/id #uuid "9c5a24fa-708c-583a-a345-c52f3aa911d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361533} {:answer/id #uuid "b26d0910-a34a-5209-9a33-b42495f6695f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361628} {:answer/id #uuid "c9642213-619d-5f39-b7b7-a194e5db904f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361747} {:answer/id #uuid "e3588d61-9553-531b-9d36-cee636d25f26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361855}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186361855} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ec73497-ac99-5d21-88bb-baefe07c1bbb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361992}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "90452d65-c7b3-548e-83d9-2c700d6e9c0f" :question/math-academy-id "q-9998" :question/problem "The entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ k & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nequals $-1.$ Find the value of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ k & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix} & =0\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix}-2\\begin{vmatrix}k & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{vmatrix}+2\\begin{vmatrix}k & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =0-2(2k-0)+2(k-0) \\\\  & =-4k+2k \\\\  & =-2k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{21}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{21} & =(-1)^{2+1}\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-(4-2) \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{12}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{21} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-2k}\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{k}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{12}^{′}=-1$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{k} & =-1 \\\\ k & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186364112 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "75cb1d88-be8f-565a-8892-48a303e64be2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 6 & -4 \\\\ 11 & 0 & -9 & 0\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364114} {:answer/id #uuid "e8e4de03-83b4-5eb7-85e7-5082d3d5faf4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\begin{vmatrix}0 & -8 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 5 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 6 & -4 \\\\ 11 & 3 & -9 & 0\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364115} {:answer/id #uuid "18a26160-0ecc-5cb6-a8e9-2502d70ef054" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}0 & -8 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 3 & 8 \\\\ 11 & 3 & 0 & -9\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364116} {:answer/id #uuid "14b9fa6f-497e-5ef2-9a76-8cd1a476c61b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\begin{vmatrix}0 & -8 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 5 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 3 & 3 \\\\ 11 & 3 & 0 & 0\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364117} {:answer/id #uuid "192fe4e1-90f7-57bb-9824-063dbac2dd60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}0 & -8 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 5 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 3 & 3 \\\\ 11 & 3 & 0 & 0\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364118}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186364117} :answer-field/id #uuid "c3453afe-00bf-5199-ac64-1a8b6d15168a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364113}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e657c376-dc40-5550-9d65-c80b82ab3edb" :question/math-academy-id "q-36048" :question/problem "Find the cofactor of ${d}_{34}$ in \n$$\n\\displaystyle D=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -8 & 2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 5 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -5 & 6 & -4 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 3 & 8 & 3 \\\\ 11 & 3 & 0 & -9 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, to get the minor of ${d}_{34}$, we remove the $3$rd row and $4$th column: \n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -8 & 2 & ∗ & -1 \\\\ 3 & 5 & 0 & ∗ & 1 \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & ∗ & 6 & ∗ \\\\ 4 & 0 & 3 & ∗ & 3 \\\\ 11 & 3 & 0 & ∗ & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, the minor is \n\n$$\n{M}_{34}=\\begin{vmatrix}0 & -8 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 5 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 3 & 3 \\\\ 11 & 3 & 0 & 0\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, the cofactor of ${d}_{34}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}_{34} & =(-1)^{3+4}{M}_{34} \\\\  & =-{M}_{34} \\\\  & =-\\begin{vmatrix}0 & -8 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 5 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 3 & 3 \\\\ 11 & 3 & 0 & 0\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186367324 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30ef06e0-089b-54f0-a23e-7a535dcf88b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}7 & 6 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 5 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 15 & -1 & -5 & 6 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 3 & 8\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367326} {:answer/id #uuid "f496b802-659a-5791-ba99-e764c38849f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 0 & 9 & 1 \\\\ 15 & -5 & 6 & -4 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 8 & 3 \\\\ 18 & 0 & -9 & -3\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367327} {:answer/id #uuid "4fb96cad-f716-53b8-bb74-5986ffa26c47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}5 & 0 & 9 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -5 & 6 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 3 & 8 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -9 & -3\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367328} {:answer/id #uuid "b7c4ed2f-07cf-5a5b-b00a-1257fb62002f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\begin{vmatrix}5 & 0 & 9 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -5 & 6 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 3 & 8 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -9 & -3\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367329} {:answer/id #uuid "811d9bf0-4181-5fb3-b9bc-1a817d08f88c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\begin{vmatrix}7 & 6 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 5 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 15 & -1 & -5 & 6 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 3 & 8\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367330}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186367326} :answer-field/id #uuid "301d66c1-40cb-5a16-aa7b-6dd3d5ee7b42" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367325}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "a9350630-2246-5e07-9684-2d3afcf4dc67" :question/math-academy-id "q-130908" :question/problem "Find the cofactor of ${q}_{55}$ in \n$$\n\\displaystyle Q=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 6 & 2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 5 & 0 & 9 & 1 \\\\ 15 & -1 & -5 & 6 & -4 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 3 & 8 & 3 \\\\ 18 & 3 & 0 & -9 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, to get the minor of ${q}_{55}$, we remove the $5$th row and $5$th column: \n\n$$\nQ=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 6 & 2 & 0 & ∗ \\\\ 3 & 5 & 0 & 9 & ∗ \\\\ 15 & -1 & -5 & 6 & ∗ \\\\ 4 & -4 & 3 & 8 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & ∗ & ∗ & -3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, the minor is \n\n$$\n{M}_{55}=\\begin{vmatrix}7 & 6 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 5 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 15 & -1 & -5 & 6 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 3 & 8\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, the cofactor of ${q}_{55}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}_{55} & =(-1)^{5+5}{M}_{55} \\\\  & ={M}_{55} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}7 & 6 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 5 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 15 & -1 & -5 & 6 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 3 & 8\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368489 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b24999b4-78f0-5329-99e0-9ca8ec99e96d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -7 & 0 & 3\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368491} {:answer/id #uuid "c6b405a1-f147-50d8-b262-948b3ef91fbe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -7 & 0 & 3\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368492} {:answer/id #uuid "bab4f45e-f87e-5831-ab73-67f9596249aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368493} {:answer/id #uuid "56b7a0be-62e3-5f15-890c-3f566007ac87" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368494} {:answer/id #uuid "09276c8d-ed02-5de7-8af1-90fbb6f4aaae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368495}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368494} :answer-field/id #uuid "5366cce4-b95c-579d-bf5b-43c029e52ab3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368490}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "55021539-024c-5816-9b9c-0adaf5b9e403" :question/math-academy-id "q-36049" :question/problem "Find the cofactor of ${c}_{21}$ in  $C=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -7 & 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we get the minor corresponding to ${c}_{21}$, removing the $2$nd row and the $1$st column:\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}∗ & 2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & ∗ & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ ∗ & 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, the minor is \n\n$$\n{M}_{21}=\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the cofactor of ${c}_{21}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}_{21} & =(-1)^{2+1}{M}_{21} \\\\  & =-{M}_{21} \\\\  & =-\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368541 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ea4df699-7d9c-5d0f-9c99-1f7c51c9eb05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "70" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368543} {:answer/id #uuid "d5501494-bc71-5997-8259-0e5ae5acb0ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368544} {:answer/id #uuid "6c10f6a2-fd34-5592-aac4-362e161f9a0c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368545} {:answer/id #uuid "93b023b1-7456-560d-a37c-931aaca0765c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368546} {:answer/id #uuid "db2b9044-1bff-57ee-ae25-64a27083c912" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368547}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368543} :answer-field/id #uuid "db95a348-0986-5700-b656-e8563530f38a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368542}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "46279f1d-0462-5a35-b644-65d4c737b0e0" :question/math-academy-id "q-40212" :question/problem "Calculate the determinant of the matrix\n$$\n\\displaystyle H=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 5 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We use the cofactor expansion along the first row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(H) & ={h}_{11}{C}_{11}+{h}_{12}{C}_{12}+{h}_{13}{C}_{13}+{h}_{14}{C}_{14} \\\\  & =2\\cdot {C}_{11}+0\\cdot {C}_{12}+(-1)\\cdot {C}_{13}+0\\cdot {C}_{14} \\\\  & =2\\cdot {C}_{11}+(-1)\\cdot {C}_{13} \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}2 & ∗ & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ ∗ & 5 & 0 & 2 \\\\ ∗ & 0 & 3 & -2\\end{vmatrix}+(-1)\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}∗ & ∗ & -1 & ∗ \\\\ 7 & 0 & ∗ & 0 \\\\ -1 & 5 & ∗ & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & ∗ & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-1)^{1+1}\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -2\\end{vmatrix}+(-1)\\cdot (-1)^{1+3}\\begin{vmatrix}7 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -2\\end{vmatrix}-\\begin{vmatrix}7 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\left(0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{vmatrix}-0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}5 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{vmatrix}+0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{vmatrix}\\right)-\\left(7\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}5 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{vmatrix}-0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{vmatrix}+0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{vmatrix}\\right) \\\\  & =2(0)-(7(-10)) \\\\  & =-(-70) \\\\  & =70\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382256 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d5a77823-c6b0-5dfd-b080-ffe4cfc11f5d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382258} {:answer/id #uuid "a381d779-2e85-5aaf-8b89-c41349f150fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382259} {:answer/id #uuid "3cb7cd1d-1fab-5c3b-9461-a541a4c58031" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382260} {:answer/id #uuid "f9757233-a669-5535-91c9-3301d2cdc860" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382261} {:answer/id #uuid "af3bcfe1-d593-5fe7-88cf-00c2b3af0a03" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382262}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382261} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf58cd3e-d1ca-5107-be49-843e76215f44" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382257}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "53b328c9-6698-53f6-9c7d-d6d44c5e77f6" :question/math-academy-id "q-73533" :question/problem "The entry ${a}_{13}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & k & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nequals $\\frac{1}{18}$ and $det(A)=-18.$ Find the value of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that we are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\ndet(A)=-18\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{13}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{31}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{31} & =(-1)^{3+1}\\begin{vmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ k & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ k & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2+k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{13}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{31} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{18}\\cdot (2+k).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{13}^{′}=\\frac{1}{18}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{18}(2+k) & =\\frac{1}{18} \\\\ 2+k & =-1 \\\\ k & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186386055 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e5a90ce-5f43-5f35-b7b8-583244a42439" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386057} {:answer/id #uuid "8602540d-4801-5042-9916-98e607f58c64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386058} {:answer/id #uuid "c57393fc-dedc-5a9b-9994-032d00d28eef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386059} {:answer/id #uuid "8bc9fb87-d9dc-5a6b-ab93-485448959e7b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386060} {:answer/id #uuid "66812ddb-563d-5415-bd8f-27772bb7e151" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386061}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186386060} :answer-field/id #uuid "e416161a-9bd1-5b5b-810d-ebf9a09026af" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386056}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "852dcdfe-ad8b-55fc-ab02-b3cb773c55c0" :question/math-academy-id "q-103533" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$\ngiven that $det(A)=4.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's follow the standard five-step procedure.\n\n**Step 1:** We are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Form the matrix of the minors of $A.$\nTo make this matrix, we replace each entry of $A$ by its minor.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{vmatrix}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Create the matrix of cofactors by changing the sign of some of the entries of $M$ according to the rule of alternating signs.\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Step 4:** Write down the transpose of the matrix of cofactors.\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Step 5:** Use the formula for the inverse of a $3\\times 3$ matrix.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388174 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7ac94783-3833-5c62-b8ff-99e49318afa8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}8 & \\sqrt{3} & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388176} {:answer/id #uuid "c9e5b38f-c2e8-543b-b00d-cd4bd8f73e6d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}1 & \\sqrt{3} & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8 \\\\ -7 & 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388177} {:answer/id #uuid "9b8b2ac7-7ee9-5860-8395-e3dfed4ac549" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 8 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 3 & 3 & 19 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388178} {:answer/id #uuid "89206cee-d78a-5591-9695-a660fc57e756" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 19 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 1 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388179} {:answer/id #uuid "aa54b09e-b6a0-545e-bd70-1a19ce8da4bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 19 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8 \\\\ -7 & 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388180}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388177} :answer-field/id #uuid "bd894676-d9a2-51c4-b3ed-225d4bfba13d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388175}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "27064447-2648-5562-9eb6-77f50dae0ce5" :question/math-academy-id "q-130822" :question/problem "What is the minor of ${q}_{22}$ in \n$$\n\\displaystyle Q=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 8 & \\sqrt{3} & -1 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 19 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 8 \\\\ -7 & 4 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To get the minor of ${q}_{22}$, we remove the $2$nd row and $2$nd column:\n\n$$\nQ=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & ∗ & \\sqrt{3} & -1 \\\\ ∗ & 3 & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ 0 & ∗ & 0 & 8 \\\\ -7 & ∗ & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, the minor is \n\n$$\n{M}_{22}=\\begin{vmatrix}1 & \\sqrt{3} & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8 \\\\ -7 & 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388188 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32af6844-5246-5136-9000-3ee064ffc19f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}8 & 2 & \\sqrt{3} & -2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & \\sqrt{7} & 1 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 6 & -4 \\\\ 11 & 0 & -9 & 11\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388190} {:answer/id #uuid "d737f210-dea9-5f09-a66e-aa69dee797b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}8 & 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -8 & -5 & -4 \\\\ 4 & \\sqrt{5} & 3 & 3 \\\\ 11 & 3 & 0 & 11\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388191} {:answer/id #uuid "b8de215d-f356-52db-9dfe-292de5b13226" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\begin{vmatrix}8 & 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -8 & -5 & -4 \\\\ 4 & \\sqrt{5} & 3 & 3 \\\\ 11 & 3 & 0 & 11\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388192} {:answer/id #uuid "792dcc1e-8af6-5018-a2ca-9221df1a6e4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 5 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -8 & -5 & -4 \\\\ 4 & \\sqrt{5} & 8 & 3 \\\\ 11 & 3 & 0 & 11\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388193} {:answer/id #uuid "1840b511-aeb2-52cf-bd75-d8d4779c7441" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\begin{vmatrix}8 & 2 & \\sqrt{3} & -2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & \\sqrt{7} & 1 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 6 & -4 \\\\ 11 & 0 & -9 & 11\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388194}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388190} :answer-field/id #uuid "f16b4332-934a-537a-8f1f-9d31b9413455" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388189}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "2ead9650-2d18-5f36-b35f-cc2f4e8392b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-130905" :question/problem "Find the cofactor of ${g}_{42}$ in \n$$\n\\displaystyle G=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 0 & 2 & \\sqrt{3} & -2 \\\\ 3 & 5 & 0 & \\sqrt{7} & 1 \\\\ 0 & -8 & -5 & 6 & -4 \\\\ 4 & \\sqrt{5} & 3 & 8 & 3 \\\\ 11 & 3 & 0 & -9 & 11\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, to get the minor of ${g}_{42}$, we remove the $4$th row and $2$nd column: \n\n$$\nG=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & ∗ & 2 & \\sqrt{3} & -2 \\\\ 3 & ∗ & 0 & \\sqrt{7} & 1 \\\\ 0 & ∗ & -5 & 6 & -4 \\\\ ∗ & \\sqrt{5} & ∗ & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ 11 & ∗ & 0 & -9 & 11\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, the minor is \n\n$$\n{M}_{42}=\\begin{vmatrix}8 & 2 & \\sqrt{3} & -2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & \\sqrt{7} & 1 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 6 & -4 \\\\ 11 & 0 & -9 & 11\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, the cofactor of ${g}_{42}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}_{42} & =(-1)^{4+2}{M}_{42} \\\\  & ={M}_{42} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}8 & 2 & \\sqrt{3} & -2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & \\sqrt{7} & 1 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 6 & -4 \\\\ 11 & 0 & -9 & 11\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 175921